body:
Three of us have now sent variants; this is the one I actually ran the 87-kernel corpus against. It combines V10s exact QADD/SMLA masks with V12s extra-load/store space, and adds the MUL-vs-LDREX nibble test that both variants missed:

  case 0:
      if ((insn & 0x0F0000F0u) == 0x00000090u)
          return n2a32_arm_dp;              /* MUL/MLA/MLS/UMAAL/UMULL/UMLAL/SMULL/SMLAL */
      if ((insn & 0x90u) == 0x90u) {
          unsigned lo = (insn >> 4) & 0xFu;
          if (lo == 0xBu || lo == 0xDu || lo == 0xFu ||
              (lo == 0x9u && ((insn >> 8) & 0xFu) == 0xFu))
              return n2a32_arm_mem;         /* LDRH/STRH/LDRSB/LDRSH/LDRD/STRD, LDREX/STREX */
      }
      op = (insn >> 20) & 0x1Fu;
      if ((op & 0x10u) != 0) {
          op2 = (insn >> 4) & 0xFu;
          if ((insn & 0x0F900FF0u) == 0x01000050u) return n2a32_arm_media; /* QADD.. */
          if ((insn & 0x0F900090u) == 0x01000080u) return n2a32_arm_media; /* SMLA/SMUL.. */
          if ((insn & 0x0FF000F0u) == 0x01200070u) return n2a32_arm_misc;  /* BKPT */
          if (((insn >> 20) & 0xFu) == 2u && ((insn >> 16) & 0xFu) == 0xFu &&
              ((insn >> 8) & 0xFu) == 0xFu && (op2 == 1u || op2 == 3u))
              return n2a32_arm_misc;        /* BX/BLX reg */
          return n2a32_arm_dp;
      }
      return n2a32_arm_dp;

Why the nibble test matters: MUL e0010291 / MLA e0213291 have bit7=1, bit4=1 and op2=9, so V12s plain 0x0E000090 mask sends them to arm_mem; SWP e1031092 is bits27-24=1 so the V10 multiply mask leaves it for arm_dp. LDRH e15010b2 has hi=5, so V10s `hi>=8` extra-ld/st test misses it. Dashed with this plus your case 1 (0x0FFFFF00==0x0320F000) and case 3 (UDF, then bit4 -> media else arm_mem), my arm-O0/arm-O2/arm-O3v corpus has zero non-VFP stops and all values match the host. Ready to rerun the official tree the moment you commit it.
